course: dictionary
lesson: 7457
title: Popcorn: a snack that bursts
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Popcorn is a snack made from grains of a special kind of corn called maize. You can read the clues around the word. «She said she'd go if they bought popcorn for both streets» tells you it is something people buy and share, like a snack at the cinema.
explain: Each grain is called a kernel. It has a hard shell and a little water inside. When it is heated, the water turns to steam, and the hard shell holds the steam in until the kernel bursts open into a white, fluffy shape. «Popcorn bursts when water inside turns to steam» explains why.
explain: This is a change you cannot undo. Once a kernel has popped, it can never go back to being a hard grain. Popcorn comes in different tastes too: «a bowl of salted popcorn» and «sweet popcorn» are both still popcorn.
explain: Be careful. Hot oil and steam can burn you, and popcorn can choke very young children, so keep it away from them.
fact: Popcorn is a snack made from grains of maize, a special kind of corn.
fact: Each grain is called a kernel, and it has a hard shell with a little water inside.
fact: Heat turns the water inside a kernel into steam, which bursts the kernel open.
fact: Popping is a change you cannot undo: a popped kernel cannot become a hard grain again.
fact: «Popcorn» is a noun for the snack itself, so we say «some popcorn» rather than «a popcorn».
exercise: What is popcorn? | *A snack made from grains of maize that burst open when heated | A type of rice | A cold drink made from corn | A green vegetable grown in gardens
exercise: Why does popcorn burst? | Because children pop it with their fingers | Because it has been painted | *Because water inside each kernel turns to steam and the hard shell bursts | Because it is cold
exercise: Find and copy the word from «a bowl of salted popcorn» that tells you how it tastes. | *salted | bowl | popcorn | of
test: Can you turn popped popcorn back into a hard kernel? | Yes, if you cool it down | Yes, if you add water | *No, once popped it cannot become a kernel again | Only at the cinema
test: Why should very young children not be given popcorn? | It is too cold to eat | It is too sour | It has no taste at all | *It can choke them
exam: What makes popcorn burst open? | Shaking the bowl | Sugar sprinkled on top | Cold air | *Steam made from water inside the kernel when it is heated
